{
  "source": "Prompts/curiosity-2.mp4",
  "duration": 200.365,
  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 3.36,
      "text": "Imagine you are the captain of your school's basketball team."
    },
    {
      "start": 4.04,
      "end": 6.86,
      "text": "You run a play that has worked perfectly all season long."
    },
    {
      "start": 7.7,
      "end": 11.22,
      "text": "Then suddenly, the opposing team figures out how to stop it."
    },
    {
      "start": 11.96,
      "end": 14.72,
      "text": "Before you find a better play, you need to be curious."
    },
    {
      "start": 15.5,
      "end": 16.88,
      "text": "You have to look at the board and ask,"
    },
    {
      "start": 17.3,
      "end": 19.06,
      "text": "what exactly are they doing differently?"
    },
    {
      "start": 19.78,
      "end": 20.46,
      "text": "Where is their opening?"
    },
    {
      "start": 21.32,
      "end": 23.42,
      "text": "And what could you learn by watching the play again?"
    },
    {
      "start": 24.72,
      "end": 28.94,
      "text": "Taking an active interest, asking questions, and exploring possibilities"
    },
    {
      "start": 28.94,
      "end": 31.38,
      "text": "reaches far beyond the basketball court."
    },
    {
      "start": 32.0,
      "end": 34.16,
      "text": "It helps you keep learning throughout your entire life,"
    },
    {
      "start": 34.76,
      "end": 36.78,
      "text": "because there is always more out there to discover."
    },
    {
      "start": 37.58,
      "end": 40.18,
      "text": "Whether you are facing a tough defense in a physical game"
    },
    {
      "start": 40.18,
      "end": 43.1,
      "text": "or dealing with a new challenge in your everyday routine,"
    },
    {
      "start": 43.74,
      "end": 46.92,
      "text": "adapting to a shifting environment requires making curiosity"
    },
    {
      "start": 46.92,
      "end": 48.9,
      "text": "your first strategic action."
    },
    {
      "start": 49.82,
      "end": 52.1,
      "text": "This chart outlines the benefits of asking questions."
    },
    {
      "start": 53.02,
      "end": 56.28,
      "text": "In this first panel, curiosity acts as your armor."
    },
    {
      "start": 57.06,
      "end": 60.9,
      "text": "Influencers, advertisers, and algorithms try to change what you think."
    },
    {
      "start": 61.48,
      "end": 64.94,
      "text": "Protect your perspectives by asking, who wants me to believe this?"
    },
    {
      "start": 65.46,
      "end": 66.08,
      "text": "What's the evidence?"
    },
    {
      "start": 66.74,
      "end": 67.04,
      "text": "What's missing?"
    },
    {
      "start": 68.28,
      "end": 70.8,
      "text": "Over on the right, curiosity kills boredom."
    },
    {
      "start": 71.58,
      "end": 73.84,
      "text": "A good question makes ordinary things interesting."
    },
    {
      "start": 74.64,
      "end": 78.36,
      "text": "Asking how a system works, why people perform a task a certain way,"
    },
    {
      "start": 78.68,
      "end": 80.02,
      "text": "or what could be done differently,"
    },
    {
      "start": 80.36,
      "end": 83.72,
      "text": "forces you to engage with the actual mechanics of the world around you."
    },
    {
      "start": 84.28,
      "end": 87.5,
      "text": "Active questioning serves as a dual-purpose survival tool."
    },
    {
      "start": 88.22,
      "end": 90.02,
      "text": "It's shield your mind from outside manipulation"
    },
    {
      "start": 90.02,
      "end": 92.88,
      "text": "while keeping it from shutting down out of apathy."
    },
    {
      "start": 93.68,
      "end": 95.7,
      "text": "Moving to the bottom left, a third benefit."
    },
    {
      "start": 96.46,
      "end": 99.9,
      "text": "Curiosity helps you grow by changing how you handle feedback."
    },
    {
      "start": 100.78,
      "end": 102.82,
      "text": "You will receive criticism throughout your life."
    },
    {
      "start": 103.6,
      "end": 104.74,
      "text": "Process it constructively."
    },
    {
      "start": 105.3,
      "end": 108.8,
      "text": "Ask what worked, what could improve, and request an example."
    },
    {
      "start": 109.72,
      "end": 111.58,
      "text": "Finally, as this last panel explains,"
    },
    {
      "start": 112.08,
      "end": 113.52,
      "text": "you can learn as you live."
    },
    {
      "start": 114.5,
      "end": 117.84,
      "text": "It is completely acceptable if you don't have your life figured out today."
    },
    {
      "start": 118.56,
      "end": 121.08,
      "text": "The best strategy is to simply stay curious."
    },
    {
      "start": 121.78,
      "end": 125.58,
      "text": "Try new things, meet people, and let the things that catch your interest"
    },
    {
      "start": 125.58,
      "end": 127.08,
      "text": "guide your very next step."
    },
    {
      "start": 127.9,
      "end": 130.42,
      "text": "Treating your daily life as an ongoing investigation"
    },
    {
      "start": 130.86,
      "end": 134.28,
      "text": "immediately relieves the pressure of needing all the answers right now."
    },
    {
      "start": 134.84,
      "end": 139.76,
      "text": "And it reframes intimidating feedback into a simple, practical roadmap for growth."
    },
    {
      "start": 140.54,
      "end": 143.68,
      "text": "We can apply this exact same framework to the rapidly shifting"
    },
    {
      "start": 143.68,
      "end": 145.22,
      "text": "landscape of artificial intelligence."
    },
    {
      "start": 146.28,
      "end": 148.48,
      "text": "New models and tools appear almost daily."
    },
    {
      "start": 149.22,
      "end": 152.16,
      "text": "You do not need to exhaust yourself chasing every single new feature."
    },
    {
      "start": 152.72,
      "end": 156.36,
      "text": "You simply need to stay curious about the updates that directly impact you."
    },
    {
      "start": 157.1,
      "end": 158.76,
      "text": "This guide outlines four habits."
    },
    {
      "start": 159.82,
      "end": 162.56,
      "text": "First, use AI regularly to notice new abilities."
    },
    {
      "start": 163.66,
      "end": 166.26,
      "text": "Second, check occasionally for updates or new buttons."
    },
    {
      "start": 167.06,
      "end": 170.26,
      "text": "Third, follow one trustworthy source to stay informed."
    },
    {
      "start": 171.32,
      "end": 176.54,
      "text": "Finally, compare findings with friends as different users notice different changes."
    },
    {
      "start": 177.4,
      "end": 182.04,
      "text": "Applying these basic habits to your software prevents technological overwhelm."
    },
    {
      "start": 182.82,
      "end": 184.96,
      "text": "They keep you fully in control of your tools,"
    },
    {
      "start": 185.56,
      "end": 188.36,
      "text": "even as the digital environment continually updates."
    },
    {
      "start": 189.56,
      "end": 193.28,
      "text": "As this final reminder says, curiosity keeps you growing."
    },
    {
      "start": 193.78,
      "end": 194.8,
      "text": "Keep asking questions."
    },
    {
      "start": 195.56,
      "end": 196.68,
      "text": "Keep learning as you live."
    }
  ],
